  clock: 5  # ff52
  nonce: ff52  # ff52
  message: "RUST LIMB CLOSED ON DEV -- recording it because commit 44cbc84610\n(2026-07-31T21:45Z, \"fix(linkers): teach type_hierarchy '::'; one home for\nmember-name separators (INV-tihim)\") landed AFTER this item's last discussion\nentry (20:34Z), so the STILL OPEN list above is stale on rust.\n\nWhat 44cbc84610 did:\n  - hypergumbo_core/member_names.py is now the single home for the\n    member-name separator vocabulary (MEMBER_NAME_SEPARATORS = (\"#\", \"::\",\n    \".\")) with a recurrence linter; type_hierarchy imports\n    member_owner/member_short_name (type_hierarchy.py:46) instead of\n    hand-rolling \"#\"/\".\" splitting.\n  - rust_trait_dispatch narrowed to inherent (non-required) methods; the\n    shared Protocol-subcategory linker now emits the method->method dispatch\n    for trait requirements. Per the owner's teach-and-narrow ruling the\n    trait-anchored edges remain for inherent methods, so the ADR-0023\n    allow-list entry stays -- legitimately, exactly per its written caveat.\n  - The interface-dispatch parity gate's rust cell is a HARD PASS (no rust\n    entry in KNOWN_HOLES; strict xfail regime means CI enforces this).\n\nRe-verified live 2026-08-01: split_member_name('MyTrait::method') ->\n('MyTrait', 'method'); type_hierarchy.py:46 imports the shared helpers; rust\nabsent from test_interface_dispatch_parity.py KNOWN_HOLES.\n\nCURRENT REMAINING CELLS (per the gate, which is the authoritative re-scope):\n  cpp      WI-nizug   consumer predicate tests the CHILD for abstractness\n  dart     WI-lahub   producer emits no inheritance edge\n  solidity INV-nosoz  consumer vocabulary ignores registry ('inherits')\n  ruby     INV-nosoz  same, 'includes' (polysemous -- needs a ruling, not a\n                      constant swap; 'includes' is also emitted by\n                      rst/meson/scss/twig for document/build inclusion)\n  elixir   WI-vitas   behaviours wholly unmodelled\n  kotlin   cause CORRECTED 2026-08-01: WI-rufub's traversal-bug premise was\n           REFUTED -- the gate's own kotlin fixture is written in the\n           one-liner style that tree_sitter_kotlin 1.1.0 fails to parse.\n           Reformat the fixture to realistic multiline and re-measure; the\n           cell may go green outright. See WI-rufub (now P3) and\n           INV-sukan-salun-lariz-japut-pavag-kadol-norot-vudig.\nphp has NO hole entry -- the php limb listed as open in the previous entry\nwas closed by the producer fixes in the PR #130/#131 commit train; the green\ngate cell on CI is the evidence.\n\nSTATUS NOTE for the owner: fields.statement as written (one home for the\nsplitting rule; type_hierarchy fires for '::'-qualified languages including\nrust) is now SATISFIED with the behavioral evidence above. The item stays\n`violated` per the 2026-07-31T17:53Z re-frame (item = the parity column;\nevery remaining cell has its own owner item). If you prefer\nadvance-and-document (L14) -- close this item and let\nWI-nizug/WI-lahub/WI-vitas/INV-nosoz/WI-rufub carry their cells -- say the\nword and it flips on the evidence already recorded here."  # ff52
