  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7832
  clock: 7  # 7832
  nonce: '7832'  # 7832
  message: "CLOSED satisfied — advance-and-document (L14), per owner delegation\n2026-08-01 (\"handle as you see fit\"). This is a verdict PARTITION, not a\nclaim that interface dispatch works everywhere.\n\nWHAT THIS ITEM'S STATEMENT DEMANDS, VERIFIED LIVE (2026-08-01, dev\n54a5f34bcc, full pipeline):\n\n  1. One home for the member-name splitting rule: member_names.py owns\n     MEMBER_NAME_SEPARATORS = (\"#\", \"::\", \".\") with a recurrence linter;\n     type_hierarchy.py:46 imports member_owner/member_short_name instead of\n     hand-rolling. The filed repro's blind case now splits:\n     split_member_name('MyTrait::method') -> ('MyTrait', 'method').\n  2. The framework-agnostic linker fires for rust: the item's own fixture\n     shape (pub trait Shape + impl Shape for Square), run through\n     run_behavior_map today, emits exactly the demanded edge —\n         dispatches_to: method:Shape::area -> method:Square::area\n     method-anchored, not trait-anchored (1 edge, probe under the session\n     scratchpad tihim-probe/).\n  3. Production-path enforcement: test_interface_dispatch_parity.py holds\n     rust as a HARD PASS (strict-xfail regime, CI-green on dev), so this\n     cannot silently regress.\n\nWHAT STAYS OPEN, EACH WITH ITS OWN OWNER (the parity gate keeps\n\"don't assume rust-only\" enforceable — cells drain independently):\n  cpp      -> WI-nizug   (consumer predicate: child-vs-parent abstractness)\n  dart     -> WI-lahub   (producer: no inheritance edge)\n  solidity -> INV-nosoz  (consumer vocabulary ignores registry)\n  ruby     -> INV-nosoz  (same, plus 'includes' polysemy ruling)\n  elixir   -> WI-vitas   (behaviours unmodelled)\n  kotlin   -> WI-rufub re-scope (gate fixture written in the grammar-\n              failing one-liner style; reformat + re-measure) and\n              INV-sukan (silent ERROR-tree output, the structural face)\n\nThe trait-anchored edges for INHERENT methods remain by the owner's\nteach-and-narrow ruling; the ADR-0023 allow-list entry stays legitimately\nper its own written caveat. Nothing in this closure touches that."  # 7832
